    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing (1952), Pearson (1993) & Kondo-Asai (1995) reaction-diffusion morphogenesis — Model fidelity to source: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Implements both Turing's (1952) Sections 8-10 linearized two-morphogen reaction-diffusion dispersion relation sigma(k^2) + discrete N=20 ring-of-cells model (L163-244, d_c=3.927051, k_c=1.118034 rad/cell, dominant mode s*=4) and Pearson's (1993) 2D periodic Gray-Scott PDE with exact Saddle-Node (4*(F+k)^2 = F) and Hopf (F_Hopf(k) where max |tr(J_0)| = 2.36e-16) bifurcation curves (L327-426). The equal-diffusion negative control (Du=Dv=0.20 at F=0.054, k=0.0616) is initialized around the exact nontrivial homogeneous steady state (U_*, V_*) and verified against the supercritical Turing state (Du=0.20, Dv=0.10, sigma=+0.00164). Backed by 4 Lean 4 theorems in `MathOfBiology.lean` Section 5." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing (1952), Pearson (1993) & Kondo-Asai (1995) reaction-diffusion morphogenesis — Morphometric validation: 75/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Upgrades 2D FFT radial power spectrum estimation with 3-point parabolic sub-bin interpolation (`_parabolic_subbin_peak`, L539-550) resolving distinct wavelengths across all four patterned regimes (k* = 10.89, 12.10, 11.89, 11.50 cycles/box; lambda* = 14.69, 13.23, 13.46, 13.92 px), compares the steady-state Turing labyrinth wavelength lambda* = 13.92 px directly against analytical lambda_c = 11.92 px (16.7% difference), quantifies Pomacanthus inter-stripe spacing (9.55 px, CV = 0.149) and Ostracion nearest-neighbor spot spacing (21.5 px), and runs a white-noise-initialized 1D Turing PDE across growing domains (`r = 0.9981` against Kondo & Asai 1995 empirical stripe counts, L672-703)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-measurement-connected-high-v-components-last-frame>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-measurement-dominant-wavelength-last-frame>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-measurement-fraction-of-pattern-pixels-changed-first-last-frame>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-measurement-ostracion-meleagris-segmented-turing-spots-dog-delaunay>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-measurement-pattern-coverage-last-frame>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-measurement-pearson-coral-labyrinth-f-0-054-k-0-0616-spectral-ring-wavenumber-k>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-measurement-pearson-mitosis-spots-f-0-028-k-0-062-connected-components-vs-coral-labyrinth>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-measurement-pomacanthus-imperator-segmented-skin-stripe-wavelength>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-measurement-steady-state-equal-diffusion-negative-control-du-dv-0-20-spectral-wavenumber-k>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-measurement-turing-1952-sec-8-9-analytical-critical-wavelength-c-2-k-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 7.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing (1952), Pearson (1993) & Kondo-Asai (1995) reaction-diffusion morphogenesis — MorphoEval overall 85.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) dual-agent evaluation of `1952-turing-morpho.py` (Gemini 4 Argon 91.9/100 + Claude Sonnet 5.5 High 79.1/100; consensus 85.5/100, up from 38.0/100 in v1). The remediated script implements Turing's (1952) Sections 8-10 two-morphogen linear dispersion relation sigma(k^2) and N=20 ring-of-cells morphogenesis (mode s*=4, lambda_c=5.62 cells); computes Pearson's (1993) exact Saddle-Node (4*(F+k)^2=F) and Hopf (max |tr(J_0)| = 2.36e-16) bifurcation curves with all 12 pattern classes (alpha through mu); pairs a genuine steady-state Turing labyrinth (F=0.054, k=0.0616, Du=0.20, Dv=0.10, sigma=+0.00164) with an equal-diffusion control (Du=Dv=0.20, std_V=1.91e-7) around the same nontrivial steady state; and segments SHA-256-locked photographs of Pomacanthus imperator skin stripes (spacing 9.55 px, CV=0.149, 22 Y-junctions) and Ostracion meleagris hexagonal spots (121 spots) alongside a white-noise-initialized 1D PDE test of Kondo & Asai's (1995) stripe-insertion law (r=0.9981). Overall 85.5/100 (faithfulness 83.2, reproducibility 90.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit b9976f8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 92, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 81, Morphometric validation 75, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 89, Reproducibility package 89. Output judged: turing_pearson_morphospace.png: rendered output of 1952-turing-morpho.py at b9976f8, image/png, 1674289 B, 2617×1806 px, artifact_sha256 4dce6f8427cdf23e4b4ac23e908910f5253d95b4a9e9f417d1720aadef17985a (sha256 4dce6f8427cdf23e4b4ac23e908910f5253d95b4a9e9f417d1720aadef17985a), spec_fingerprint 457ba1d8776c5109e7d828595ec1ea637e0d9b8eebcf725fc073d1f70566f695. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 457ba1d8776c5109e7d828595ec1ea637e0d9b8eebcf725fc073d1f70566f695; artifact_sha256: 4dce6f8427cdf23e4b4ac23e908910f5253d95b4a9e9f417d1720aadef17985a." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add manual ground-truth landmark annotations for Pomacanthus imperator Y-junction coordinates to benchmark automated skeleton junction recall and precision.",
        "remediation needed: Calibrate a 2D growing-domain PDE simulation with adiabatic domain expansion L(t) to observe spontaneous Y-branch stripe insertion events in 2D space-time." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.55e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-turing-gray-scott-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing (1952), Pearson (1993) & Kondo-Asai (1995) reaction-diffusion morphogenesis — Parameter expressivity: 81/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Maps all 12 Pearson (1993) pattern classes (alpha through mu) onto the (k, F) bifurcation diagram (Panel C2), simulates 5 distinct initialization/parameter regimes in `PEARSON_REGIMES`, executes a 5-point diffusivity-ratio sweep across d = Du/Dv in {1.0, 1.25, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5} (`run_diffusivity_ratio_sweep`, L515-536) spanning the analytical Turing threshold, and wires `--F`, `--k`, `--Du`, `--Dv`, `--N`, `--steps`, and `--seed` CLI arguments into the solver (L939-954, L1385-1425)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
